  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "english-poetry-anthology-s0009-p00026",
      "source_en": "I heard you solemn-sweet pipes of the organ as last Sunday morn I pass'd the church,\nWinds of autumn, as I walk'd the woods at dusk I heard your long-stretch'd sighs up above so mournful,\nI heard the perfect Italian tenor singing at the opera, I heard the soprano in the midst of the quarter singing;\nHeart of my love! you too I heard murmuring low through one of the wrists around my head,\nHeard the pulse of you when all was still ringing little bells last night under my ear.",
